Hamburg Airlines – Route Evaluation & Market Research
Overview
This market research and data analytics project evaluates flight routes and airport passenger volumes across European secondary hubs to identify underserved routes and commercial growth opportunities for Hamburg Airlines.

Key Analysis Parameters
Target Airport Segment: Mid-tier commercial passenger hubs
Passenger Volume Band: 10,000 to 40,000 mean passenger volume per period
Route Capacity: 10 to 200 operational flight routes
Geographic Scope: European hubs and Schengen countries 
Tech Stack
Languages & Frameworks: Python 3.x, Jupyter Notebook
Data Manipulation & Requests: Pandas, Requests (API-Ninjas Airports endpoint)
Data Visualization & Mapping: Matplotlib, Seaborn, Plotly (Scattergeo route mapping)
Presentation: Google Slides


Data Files (data/)
airports.csv: Global and European airport reference dataset containing IATA/ICAO codes, geographic coordinates, and metadata.
estat_ttr00017 (1).tsv: Raw Eurostat air passenger transport time-series dataset.
clean_air_traffic_2025.csv: Cleaned flight frequencies and air traffic flow metrics.
clean_passengers.csv: Cleaned passenger volume statistics across European commercial airports.
clean_routes.csv: Cleaned origin-destination airport route pairs and operational network data.
Notebooks & Scripts (notebooks/)
API.ipynb: Route mapping script fetching airport coordinates (latitude and longitude) by IATA code via API-Ninjas, generating interactive flight path visualizations with Plotly Scattergeo (e.g., HER to MAD).
Wrangling_Final.ipynb: Data cleaning, standardizing IATA airport codes, reshaping Eurostat TSV data, and merging datasets.
Analysis_Final.ipynb: Exploratory data analysis, threshold filtering (mid-tier hubs: 10k–40k passengers, 10–200 routes), statistical aggregations, and high-resolution chart exports.
Deliverables & Visualizations
Hamburg Airlines - New Route - Market Research.gslides: Executive presentation deck detailing route gap evaluation and route recommendations.
Execution Workflow
API Ingestion & Geospatial Mapping: Execute API.ipynb to retrieve airport coordinates for target IATA origin-destination pairs and plot flight routes using Plotly.
Data Wrangling: Run Wrangling_Final.ipynb to transform estat_ttr00017 (1).tsv and airports.csv into the cleaned CSV datasets (clean_air_traffic_2025.csv, clean_passengers.csv, clean_routes.csv).
Market Analysis & Visualizations: Execute Analysis_Final.ipynb to filter mid-tier passenger volume and route criteria, mapping IATA codes to standardized names and generating publication-ready figures.
Strategy Synthesis: Compile findings and route recommendations into Hamburg Airlines - New Route - Market Research.
